.sp
As well as turning on the \fBPCRE2_UTF\fP option, the \f(CRutf\fP modifier causes all
non\-printing characters in output strings to be printed using the \(rsx{hh...}
notation. Otherwise, those less than 0x100 are output in hex without the curly
brackets. Setting \f(CRutf\fP in 16\-bit or 32\-bit mode also causes pattern and
subject strings to be translated to UTF\-16 or UTF\-32, respectively, before
being passed to library functions.
.sp
The following modifiers enable or disable performance optimizations by
calling pcre2_set_optimize() before invoking the regex compiler.
.sp
.RS 4
.PD 0
